abstract: >
  This repository contains the source code, build files, camera-adapter scripts,
  and documentation for open-source Raspberry Pi 5 edge software for live thermal
  image acquisition and multithreshold segmentation. The system
  integrates a Waveshare Thermal Camera HAT (B) / MI48 thermal camera with a
  Python SPI/I2C acquisition adapter, a PySide6 graphical interface, and a C++17/OpenCV segmentation engine.
  Captured thermal frames can be processed using seven metaheuristic optimizers:
  Differential Evolution, Differential Evolution-Salp Swarm hybrid, Scheduled
  Differential Evolution, Grey Wolf Optimizer, Particle Swarm Optimization, Crow
  Search Algorithm, and Firefly Algorithm.
keywords:
  - Raspberry Pi 5
  - thermal imaging
  - multithreshold segmentation
  - edge computing
  - OpenCV
  - metaheuristic optimization
  - Kapur entropy
  - Waveshare Thermal Camera HAT
  - MI48
